  <name>Popamp</name>
  <summary>Winamp-style skinnable audio player</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Popamp is a desktop music player in the spirit of Winamp 2: a main
      window, a 10-band equalizer and a playlist that snap together, and a
      different look whenever you want one.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Its own skins are drawn as vectors and stay sharp at any size, from x1 to x3.</li>
      <li>Opens classic .wsz skins, and installs skins from the Winamp Skin Museum and the popamp.app gallery.</li>
      <li>Gapless playback, ReplayGain, an equalizer with .eqf presets and internet radio.</li>
      <li>Plays MP3, AAC, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, WAV, ALAC, MIDI, tracker modules and more.</li>
      <li>Media keys and the desktop's player controls through MPRIS.</li>
      <li>Toolbar mode turns the player into a strip along the top or bottom of the screen.</li>
      <li>No account, no cloud, no library to import.</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">popamp.desktop</launchable>
